remote: This is a WT-managed development environment for a coding agent.
remote: The developer's SSH keys and GitHub or GitLab credentials are not available here.
remote: Do not look for credentials or use gh or glab.
remote: WT gives you scoped access to project group/project.
remote: Use normal Git for commits, fetches, pulls, and pushes.
remote: Every WT world for this project can write branches under wt/.
remote: Pull or merge requests target main.
remote: ag-git is the installed CLI for pull or merge requests, reviews, and CI.
remote: Run ag-git for the current branch's status and suggested next actions.
remote: Run ag-git --help to discover every available command.
